") Parameters Type Name Description string value The string to normalize. Must not be null. string newline The replacement line terminator. Defaults to "
" (LF). May be empty to strip all line endings. Must not be null. Returns Type Description string A new string in which every recognised line ending in value has been replaced by newline. When value contains no line endings, the original instance is returned unchanged. Remarks CRLF pairs are treated as a single line ending and replaced by exactly one newline. Other Unicode line separators (U+2028, U+2029, NEL U+0085) are not touched. Exceptions Type Condition ArgumentNullException Thrown when value or newline is null.

api/Bodu.Extensions.StringExtensions.htm.summary:
Class StringExtensions Provides ergonomic, allocation-aware extension methods on string that fill gaps in the BCL — positive-form null/empty predicates, fluent fallbacks, whitespace and line-ending normalisation, affix management, substring windowing, case conversion, identifier sanitisation, and generic parsing. Inheritance object StringExtensions Inherited Members object.Equals(object) object.Equals(object, object) object.GetHashCode() object.GetType() object.MemberwiseClone() object.ReferenceEquals(object, object) object.ToString() Namespace: Bodu.Extensions Assembly: Bodu.Core.dll Syntax public static class StringExtensions Remarks Members are split across partial files following the repository convention (see CLAUDE.md): one partial file per method, named StringExtensions.<MethodName>.cs. Tests follow the same pattern under test/Extensions/StringExtensionsTests.<MethodName>.cs. Methods that conceptually deserve a place but are already short, idiomatic, or covered by the BCL are intentionally omitted (for example IsNullOrEmpty, Left / Right, Mid, ToLowerInvariant). The accompanying design document records the rationale per method. Casing methods use InvariantCulture by default so output is deterministic across machines; cultural variants are not provided to discourage accidental CurrentCulture coupling. Comparison helpers default to Ordinal for the same reason. Examples // Sanitise then truncate user input for a log line. string? raw = request?.Title; string display = raw.TrimToNull()?.CollapseWhitespace().Truncate(80, "…") ?? "(untitled)"; // Build a slug for a URL. string slug = "Hello, World! — café".ToSlug(); // "hello-world-cafe" // Round-trip identifiers between conventions. string pascal = "user_account_id".ToPascalCase(); // "UserAccountId" string snake = "UserAccountId".ToSnakeCase(); // "user_account_id" Methods Name Description After(string, string, StringComparison) Returns the substring of value following the first occurrence of marker. AfterLast(string, string, StringComparison) Returns the substring of value following the last occurrence of marker. Before(string, string, StringComparison) Returns the substring of value preceding the first occurrence of marker. BeforeLast(string, string, StringComparison) Returns the substring of value preceding the last occurrence of marker. Between(string, string, string, StringComparison) Returns the substring of value between the first occurrence of start and the next occurrence of end after it. Brace(string) Returns value wrapped in curly-brace characters ({…}). Bracket(string) Returns value wrapped in square-bracket characters ([…]). CollapseWhitespace(string) Returns value with every run of one or more white-space characters collapsed to a single space character (U+0020). ContainsOrdinalIgnoreCase(string, string) Returns a value indicating whether value contains valueToFind under OrdinalIgnoreCase. DefaultIfNullOrEmpty(string?, string) Returns defaultValue when value is null or empty; otherwise returns value unchanged. DefaultIfNullOrWhiteSpace(string?, string) Returns defaultValue when value is null, empty, or white-space-only; otherwise returns value unchanged. EndsWithOrdinal(string, string) Returns a value indicating whether value ends with valueToFind under Ordinal. EndsWithOrdinalIgnoreCase(string, string) Returns a value indicating whether value ends with valueToFind under OrdinalIgnoreCase. EnsureEndsWith(string, string, StringComparison) Returns value guaranteed to end with suffix, appending the suffix only when it is not already present. EnsureStartsWith(string, string, StringComparison) Returns value guaranteed to begin with prefix, prepending the prefix only when it is not already present. EnsureTrailingNewLine(string, string) Returns value guaranteed to end with newline, appending the terminator only when it is not already present. EqualsOrdinalIgnoreCase(string?, string?) Returns a value indicating whether value equals other under OrdinalIgnoreCase. FromBase64ToString(string, Encoding?) Decodes the Base64-encoded value back into a string using encoding (or UTF8 when encoding is null) to interpret the decoded bytes. HasText(string?) Returns a value indicating whether value is non-null, non-empty, and contains at least one character that is not white space. Indent(string, int, char) Returns value with count copies of indentChar prepended to every line. IsOneOf(string, IEqualityComparer<string>, params string[]) Returns a value indicating whether value equals any element of values under the rule supplied by comparer. IsOneOf(string, params string[]) Returns a value indicating whether value equals any element of values under ordinal comparison. IsValidIdentifier(string) Returns a value indicating whether value is a syntactically valid C# identifier (a letter or underscore followed by zero or more letters, digits, underscores, or connector punctuation). KeepDigits(string) Returns value filtered down to its Unicode digit characters. KeepLetters(string) Returns value filtered down to its Unicode letter characters. KeepLettersAndDigits(string) Returns value filtered down to its Unicode letter and digit characters. KeepWhere(string, Func<char, bool>) Returns value filtered down to the characters for which predicate returns true. NormalizeLineEndings(string, string) Returns value with every CRLF (
