d representation of value after encoding it with encoding (or UTF8 when encoding is null). ToCamelCase(string) Converts value to camelCase: the first word is lower-cased and each subsequent word has its first character upper-cased, with separators removed. ToCamelCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to camelCase under the supplied options. ToConstantCase(string) Converts value to CONSTANT_CASE: upper-cased words joined by underscores. ToConstantCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to CONSTANT_CASE under the supplied options. ToDotCase(string) Converts value to dot.case: lower-cased words joined by periods. ToDotCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to dot.case under the supplied options. ToIdentifier(string) Converts value into a syntactically valid C# identifier by removing characters that are not permitted in identifiers and preserving the original casing of the remaining characters. ToIdentifier(string, IdentifierCase) Converts value into a syntactically valid C# identifier and reshapes the detected words to identifierCase. ToKebabCase(string) Converts value to kebab-case: lower-cased words joined by hyphens. ToKebabCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to kebab-case under the supplied options. ToPascalCase(string) Converts value to PascalCase: every word has its first character upper-cased and the remaining characters lower-cased, with separators removed. ToPascalCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to PascalCase under the supplied options. ToSafeFileName(string) Returns value with every character that GetInvalidFileNameChars() reports as invalid for a file name replaced by an underscore. ToSafePathSegment(string) Returns value with every character that GetInvalidFileNameChars() reports as invalid for a single path segment (plus the platform path separators) replaced by an underscore. ToSentenceCase(string) Returns value with the first letter of every sentence capitalised and every other letter lower-cased, using InvariantCulture. ToSentenceCase(string, SentenceCaseOptions) Returns value in sentence case under the supplied options. ToSentenceCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Returns value in sentence case under the supplied options, applying acronym-aware tokenisation, mixed-case-word preservation, and culture-sensitive casing. ToSlug(string) Converts value to a URL-friendly slug: lower-cased words joined by hyphens with diacritics normalised and punctuation removed. ToSlug(string, SlugOptions) Converts value to a URL-friendly slug under the supplied options. ToSnakeCase(string) Converts value to snake_case: lower-cased words joined by underscores. ToSnakeCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to snake_case under the supplied options. ToTitleCase(string) Returns value with the first character of every word capitalised and the rest lower-cased, using InvariantCulture. ToTitleCase(string, TitleCaseOptions) Returns value in title case under the supplied options. ToTitleCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Returns value in title case under the supplied options, applying acronym-aware tokenisation, mixed-case-word preservation, and culture-sensitive casing. ToTrainCase(string) Converts value to Train-Case: each word has its first character upper-cased and the rest lower-cased, joined by hyphens. ToTrainCase(string, WordCasingOptions) Converts value to Train-Case under the supplied options. TrimOrEmpty(string?) Returns the trimmed form of value, or Empty when value is null. TrimToNull(string?) Returns the trimmed form of value, or null when value is null or the trimmed result is empty. Truncate(string, int) Returns value truncated to at most maxLength characters. Truncate(string, int, string) Returns value truncated to at most maxLength characters, appending ellipsis to indicate truncation. TruncateMiddle(string, int, string) Returns value truncated to at most maxLength characters by keeping the beginning and end intact and inserting separator in the middle. TryParseSpan<T>(string, out T) Attempts to parse value into the requested T using the ISpanParsable<TSelf> contract and InvariantCulture, routing through the underlying character span. TryParse<T>(string, out T) Attempts to parse value into the requested T using the IParsable<TSelf> contract and InvariantCulture. UnprefixLines(string, string) Returns value with one occurrence of prefix removed from the start of every line that begins with it. Unwrap(string, string, string, StringComparison) Returns value with prefix and suffix removed if both are present at their respective ends. Wrap(string, string, string) Returns value with prefix prepended and suffix appended.
